### Docker vs Podman in your case

Think of it this way:

```text
DOCKER
docker run ...
     |
     v
Docker CLI
     |
     v
Docker Daemon (dockerd)  <-- must keep running
     |
     v
Container
```

```text
PODMAN
podman run ...
     |
     v
Container runtime
     |
     v
Container

No permanent central daemon required
```

Podman is OCI-compatible and deliberately supports a Docker-like CLI. More importantly for a corporate laptop, **Podman can run rootless**, which means you don't necessarily need a privileged Docker daemon running all the time. ([Podman Documentation][1])

And there's particularly good news for you: **IBM explicitly supports running the MQ container with Podman**, and IBM's MQ container documentation literally says you can substitute `podman` for `docker` in its examples. ([GitHub][2])

So for:

```text
Spring Boot development
       |
       +---- IBM MQ container :1414
       |
       +---- Kafka container :9092
```

Podman is completely reasonable.

